# Overlap is not only two identical entries. A task owning a directory owns
# everything under it, so a second task owning a file inside it is claimable at
# the same time as the first and would edit the same tree. The trailing slash
# WORKPLAN.md writes a directory with is not what makes it one, so it is
# stripped before the comparison rather than compared.
run available
exit 3
file tasks/M1-01.md
	---
	id: M1-01
	owns:
	  - crates/
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
file tasks/M1-02.md
	---
	id: M1-02
	owns:
	  - crates/normalize/src/lib.rs
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
stderr
	tasks.sh: tasks/M1-02.md: owns crates/normalize/src/lib.rs, which overlaps the crates/ that M1-01 owns, and neither depends on the other
